  blockTitle: 'AT 173: Corinthian Column Capital'
  blockDescription: Column capital, the best preserved of the four original ones.
    The capital is of the corinthian genus, bearing stylized acanthus leaves and
    tendrils in the corners and the middle part of the capital. The corinthian order
    was commonly used in Imperial Roman Architecture, as the most ornate order.
  blockPlacement: "The pediment block was found at the southwest of the temple, and
    is restored at the front fa\xE7ade of the temple."
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 0}
  blockDrawing2: {fileID: 0}
